uid "5cb2afb1-bc85-553a-b1f5-353aae32076d" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283805 1034 "n=\\pm 4" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283805 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283805 1111 #uuid "50067a03-1333-5bf0-a22b-1f89881465a1" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283806 1034 "n=4" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283806 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283806 1111 #uuid "9e763788-e014-5dfe-bb78-d0e0a7d97e3f" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283807 1034 "n=\\pm 2" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283807 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283807 1111 #uuid "668cc876-46ae-5a7a-9648-0751b3caf48d" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283808 1034 "n=-2" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283808 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283808 1111 #uuid "9ba2c3f7-d9cd-5fe9-a1ed-affd720daeb3" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283809 1034 "n=-4" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283809 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283809 1111 #uuid "d1a29f37-a243-5c17-a6f7-dff248983c9f" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283810 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283811 13194139534345 true] [17592186283810 1089 "q-127821" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283810 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534345 true] [17592186283810 1100 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283810 1113 #uuid "41a5decc-6a63-5e15-9219-32df767b7987" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283810 1145 "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 5-7\\cdot 0=5.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283812 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283813 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283814 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283815 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283816 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1041 "selection" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283813 13194139534345 true] [17592186283811 1110 #uuid "cca04b2b-a4de-5524-b216-2806fb864de7" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283812 1034 "$B$  and $C$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283812 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283812 1111 #uuid "22f462bf-af92-5f66-b161-1437e27ac16d" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283813 1034 "$A$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283813 1111 #uuid "6f1e8475-4581-5d54-82c8-30a79f5b84c3" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283814 1034 "$A$  and $C$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283814 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283814 1111 #uuid "bfd23f33-7e15-58a1-8b3c-cfba4dd114bd" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283815 1034 "$C$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283815 1111 #uuid "2fa270f1-39b7-5559-91a0-c3ac999965f0" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283816 1034 "$B$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283816 1111 #uuid "dfd5b2c0-51ad-5626-9b43-54b1a0d7fccf" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283817 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283818 13194139534345 true] [17592186283817 1089 "q-127901" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283817 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534345 true] [17592186283817 1100 "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}48 & a \\\\ a & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $a.$" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283817 1113 #uuid "67bc8ab5-c4a7-53b0-b9d4-1ed70d9f6dbd" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283817 1145 "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =48\\cdot 3-a\\cdot a \\\\  & =144-{a}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}144-{a}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =144 \\\\ a & =\\pm 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $a$ are $a=\\pm 12.$" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283819 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283820 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283821 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283822 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283823 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1041 "selection" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283822 13194139534345 true] [17592186283818 1110 #uuid "0fa4888e-ae52-58a0-a416-fe73c97693b1" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283819 1034 "a=\\pm 4" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283819 1111 #uuid "a8f3bf97-bbd7-501a-982e-40be88e617cb" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283820 1034 "a=\\pm 9" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283820 1111 #uuid "2e5aa331-8ed7-5b85-9d2e-bf04adc39ae5" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283821 1034 "a=1" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283821 1111 #uuid "0efe0cfa-da0f-52d3-95a8-480613bdc19e" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283822 1034 "a=\\pm 12" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283822 1111 #uuid "8fa8fe29-70c0-52bc-9ed1-8d885a0128bd" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283823 1034 "a=2" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283823 1111 #uuid "f3d62c9d-06c5-5717-842b-2ffa2f92a7d4" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283824 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283825 13194139534345 true] [17592186283824 1089 "q-275738" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283824 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534345 true] [17592186283824 1100 "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}x-5 & x+3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283824 1113 #uuid "1001d893-ecd0-5002-87f8-aa27a5a9e78c" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283824 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-5)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (x+3) \\\\  & =-3x+15-2x-6 \\\\  & =-5x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283826 13194139534345 true] [17592186283825 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534345 true] [17592186283825 1041 "field-1" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283825 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283826 13194139534345 true] [17592186283825 1110 #uuid "219788c3-5b8c-5404-a253-21c37bcbc3cf" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283826 1034 "\\frac{9}{5}" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283826 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534345 true] [17592186283826 1111 #uuid "d44a3b5c-10eb-5340-9c5e-b15d0cb24b3b" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283827 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283828 13194139534345 true] [17592186283827 1089 "q-7923" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283827 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534345 true] [17592186283827 1100 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,G=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283827 1113 #uuid "e1200f5c-4446-5343-a392-4a0d1b7415e1" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283827 1145 "- For the matrix $D$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(D)=3\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(D)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $D$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $F$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(F)=6\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(F)=0,$ we conclude that $F$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $G$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(G)=(-2)\\cdot 4-4\\cdot 2=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(G)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $G$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ does not have an inverse." 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283829 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283830 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283831 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283832 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283833 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1041 "selection" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283830 13194139534345 true] [17592186283828 1110 #uuid "5f0956b5-0f62-5fe0-afd9-ac75f12da804" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283829 1034 "$D$ and $F$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283829 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283829 1111 #uuid "a7d03e0d-dd0b-5bf2-8b23-b76ba4a52cb8" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283830 1034 "$F$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283830 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283830 1111 #uuid "31e64cc4-7607-5320-b4ee-b148069f834c" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283831 1034 "$F$ and $G$ only" 13194139534345 true] [17592186283831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534345 true] [17592186283831 1111 #uuid "11647ab9-20e9-5f5d-8ca6-1654dff9013b" 1319413953